Lumen OS: Wi-Fi Direct on vendors whose supplicant reports AIDL V3 from a snapshot taken before V3 froze.

The MediaTek TV vendors of XGIMI projectors (Z9X G0082 v61519/v61558/v61562, X50 Ultra G0111, TITAN H0062 v1.2.54
and v1.2.99: one 64-bit file, RS30 Ultra Max G0155: its 32-bit build) ship android.hardware.wifi.supplicant-V3-ndk.so
with interface hash 4652398bc565e185ec0799d2a9ea9db1774710bc, not the frozen V3 55b58c9bd6d40c1459073b5d03f4ede5cfc9a212.
Its ISupplicantP2pIface has the 63 V2 calls at their frozen transaction codes, a vendor call
(startWpsPinKeypadWithMac) at code 64, where frozen V3 has connectWithParams, and nothing above it (proven from the
Bp transact codes and the Bn onTransact jump table of the library). getInterfaceVersion() still answers 3, so this
framework sends configureExtListenWithParams (code 66) for WifiP2pManager.startListening and connectWithParams
(code 64) for every connection it accepts. The first fails as unimplemented, handleRemoteException drops the P2P
interface and every later P2P call fails ("Can't call find, ISupplicantP2pIface is null"); the second would run the
vendor call with a P2pConnectInfo parcel. A fallback on "unimplemented" alone cannot catch the second one.
The P2P HAL now decides each V3 call from the interface hash (SupplicantP2pV3Calls): only the frozen V3 hash gets
connectWithParams, findWithParams and configureExtListenWithParams, any other hash gets the V2 calls connect, find
and configureExtListen, which every snapshot keeps at their frozen codes. A V3 call that still answers unimplemented
is switched off for the life of the interface and the V2 call is made instead of dropping the interface.
Device-neutral: supplicants that report V1 or V2, and frozen V3 ones, get exactly the calls they got before.

